cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the journal article (once published) and this repository."
title: "UAV-swarm distributed-aperture reception of LEO satellites - simulation code and data"
abstract: >-
  Closed-loop simulator, reference generator and analysis scripts for a study of
  UAV-swarm distributed-aperture reception of non-cooperative LEO satellites. Two
  stages are included. The second identifies and proves a failure mode of the
  rate-limited reference direction used to score controllers, shows that its lag
  grows without bound whenever the instantaneous optimum migrates faster than the
  array can turn, and replaces it with an exact rate-constrained optimal reference
  computed by dynamic programming on the periodic orientation circle. Correcting the
  reference shifts the reported aperture gains differentially, strengthening the
  earlier conclusion rather than undermining it. The first stage provides the
  closed-loop comparison itself, a length-controlled alignment metric, a
  connectivity-aperture trade-off analysis, a per-step compute budget and a
  three-site robustness check. Every aggregate result table, the figure scripts and
  a number-verification script are included.
